FALL FTW // Our All Balanchine I program showcased the immense breadth of George Balanchine’s choreography through four completely distinct ballets. Opening with the hauntingly romantic La Sonnambula, the program segued into more avant-garde works, Pithoprakta and The Unanswered Question, before finishing with his bright and classical Theme and Variations, a technical tour de force.

See a triple bill of more Balanchine favorites—including Mozartiana, Agon, and Tschaikovsky Piano Concerto No. 2— by securing seats to our All Balanchine II program this winter. Visit nycballet.com/allbalanchine2 for tickets. 

@taylor___stanley @naomicorti @unityphelan @davidericc @mira_nadon @ashleylaracey @cainan.weber @notjosephgordonlevitt @indiana_woodward #balanchine #nycballet #nycb #newyorkcityballet #ballet

kó's solo exhibition of Ruth Ige, "Woven realms," is open through November 21. kó is open daily, Tuesday-Sunday, 11 AM-6 PM, during Art X Lagos week. 

Ruth Ige employs a rich palette of indigo and blue to depict enigmatic female figures suspended between portraiture and imagined landscapes, drawing upon African cultural traditions and ideas of identity, spirituality, and protection. Her paintings construct mythical spaces where silhouetted figures, predominantly women, inhabit worlds that feel at once earthly and otherworldly. The exhibition was recently reviewed in Artforum (October 2026). 

@ruth_ige_art

Art X Lagos is two days away! kó is pleased to participate in Art X Lagos, November 5-8 2026, with a multigenerational 
presentation of artists across Nigerian modernism and contemporary practice. This presentation includes pioneering modernists including Ben Enwonwu, Obiora Udechukwu, and Tayo Adenaike, who work enter dialogue with contemporary artists including Marcia Kure, Ozioma Onuzulike, Ngozi-Omeje Ezema, Ruth Ige, Abdus Salaam, Ayotunde Ojo, and Diana Ejaita. 

@artxlagos

- Oscaar Mouligne Gallery Kyoto - 
show opens November 7 thru March 6 2027 
  @oscaar.mouligne // LORNA SIMPSON

@jamielloydco’s revival of “Much Ado About Nothing” is now in previews! 🩷
Tom Hiddleston (@twhiddleston) and Hayley Atwell (@wellhayley) star in @thetonyawards winner Jamie Lloyd’s reinvention of William Shakespeare’s giddily funny and beautifully tender battle of wits.
”Much Ado About Nothing” - Winter Garden Theatre Written by William Shakespeare Directed by Jamie Lloyd Choreographed by Fabian Aloise

FALL FTW // A study in style and sensibility: this fall’s Eclectic NYCB I program brought together Christopher Wheeldon’s Continuum, Artist in Residence Alexei Ratmansky’s Solitude, and George Balanchine’s Bourrée Fantasque for a triple bill showcasing a range of choreographic perspectives. 

Explore repertory showcased this upcoming winter at nycballet.com/winter, performances open January 19 with the New York City Ballet premiere of Ratmansky’s Romeo & Juliet. 

@wheeldony @alexeiratmansky #balanchine #nycb #nycballet #newyorkcityballet
